WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.600
 None of that is true of course. Some of you may have believed it. No proof is

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.000
 more diverse than the average.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.000
 As you know, we have all the papers and not the papers.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:24.000
 Well, as a St. Edward alumnus, this is a great honor for me to find my glasses.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.100
 A great honor for me to introduce our most, our most revered alumnus, Jack Kahl,

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.520
 whose fingerprints are on every success our school has achieved in its many

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.000
 years of existence.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.920
 Thumbnail sketch, Jack is a self-made millionaire who is proud of his humble

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.000
 beginnings in the projects on the west side.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.560
 After graduating from St. Ed's, Jack went on to be John Farrell, and upon

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:53.000
 graduating, he ended the business world, selling duct tape.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:58.700
 He really believed in the product, and eventually he bought the company which

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.000
 became Manko.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.000
 Subsequently, he and Sam Walton became acquainted.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:11.830
 They believed in each other, which led to Manko tape being the only duct tape

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:16.000
 sold in every Walmart store in the country.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:24.150
 As Walmart became bigger, so did Manko. Although Jack became a multi-millionaire,

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:28.000
 and he became a philanthropist of heroic proportions.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:33.360
 Pecano's name was on a building at John Carroll, and on a major addition at St.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.000
 Ed's.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.320
 Jack served on the St. Edward Board of Trustees for 25 years, and now his two

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.000
 sons are on the board.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:48.000
 Whoever St. Ed's needs something, the Cale family is on their speed dialing.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.460
 Jack is now 75, and his five children and 14 grandchildren all live within five

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.000
 minutes of it.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.000
 Now he's less than a minute away from us.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.000
 Probably let me say, here's Jack Cale.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:14.000
 [applause]

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:35.000
 Jack, would you remind everybody that I have the books in the trunk of my car,

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.000
 for only $15.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:40.000
 I think you just did.

